h loving and true who acts  in our lives as mostly liberal  Christians if I can generalize we're  tempted to run away from religious rules  or a personal God and dive towards  values or ethics ethics lets us reach  out to a secular world and find our  place without that messy specificity if  we are good people they don't need to  think about God right because God is  love right but the vine and the branches  one tells us finally grow out of one  root and without connection to that  route we cannot grow in my backyard in  Pennsylvania I had trumpet vines that  would take over once a year completely  take over the wall the yard the house  the house next door they grew everywhere  up the walls over the fences ranching  over a 4-foot gap from the wall to the  roof and everywhere luxuriant foliage  and these big bright orange flowers and  I would cut them back and cut them back  trying to rescue the house and the other  plants in the yard but the only way to  battle them I finally discovered it's  not to clip each branch but to trace all  the branches back under the foliage  almost under the ground along the wall  and finally that big gnarled trunk and  take my hacksaw and saw it through our  lives our loves our actions may be  luxuriant and full but only if they're  rooted in the vine and if we are cut off  no matter how huge the branches or  bright the flowers in a day they will  wither and fall abstract love or  goodness is easier than struggling with  the irrational elements and ugly history  of the Christian story but abstract  goodness is rooted in the air in  sentiment and momentary utility and is  swept away in a moment we are called to  abide in and struggle with Christ as we  do with those closest to us staying  connected to God it's not easy these  days but every day that we embrace that  connection is a day of growth and  flowering a day when we know we are  truly known and truly loved by God who  has loved us enough to become one of us  whenever I hear the w